OxRefine is an independent reimplementation of the OpenRefine data-cleaning
workflow (https://openrefine.org). It reads and writes OpenRefine's operation
history JSON and aims to reproduce OpenRefine's results. OpenRefine is
Copyright (c) 2010 Google Inc. and 2018-present OpenRefine contributors,
licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License. OxRefine contains no OpenRefine code.
Test fixtures under tests/ were produced by running OpenRefine 3.10.1, and the
GREL function descriptions in ui/src/grel-docs.json come from OpenRefine 3.10.1
(get-expression-language-info), used under the same BSD 3-Clause License.

The small species and surveys CSV excerpts under tests/recipes/ come from the
Portal Project Teaching Database by Morgan Ernest, James Brown, Thomas Valone
and Ethan P. White (https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.1314459), released under
CC0-1.0. tests/recipes/sources.json records the exact repository revision and
selection. The accompanying recipes and modified-input scenarios were authored
for OxRefine's tests; they are not user-submitted workflows.

crates/ox-core/assets/commons-codec/ holds the Beider-Morse and Daitch-Mokotoff
rule files from Apache Commons Codec 1.20.0 (the version OpenRefine 3.10.1
uses), under the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE.txt in that folder):

  Apache Commons Codec
  Copyright 2002-2025 The Apache Software Foundation

  This product includes software developed at
  The Apache Software Foundation (https://www.apache.org/).

crates/ox-core/src/double_metaphone.rs is adapted from rphonetic 4.0.0
(https://github.com/Dalvany/rphonetic, Apache License 2.0), a port of Apache
Commons Codec's DoubleMetaphone; the changes are described at its top.

crates/ox-core/src/ppm.rs reproduces the PPM distance OpenRefine 3.10.1 uses for
nearest-neighbour clustering: vicino 1.2.1's PPMDistance (the SIMILE project, MIT)
over arithcode 1.2's order-8 PPM model and arithmetic coder (Bob Carpenter), both
bundled with OpenRefine. It was written from the behaviour of those compiled
classes, quirks included, and is checked against them (tests/cluster/ppm-gen.mjs).

crates/ox-core/src/metaphone3.rs is adapted from the metaphone3 crate 0.2.0
(https://github.com/kakserpom/metaphone3-rs, MIT License), a port of Lawrence
Philips' Metaphone 3 (BSD License); the changes are described at its top.

crates/ox-core/assets/language-detector/ contains the 70 unmodified normal
profiles from Optimaize language-detector 0.6, under Apache License 2.0.
LICENSE.txt, UPSTREAM-README.md and CREDITS.md retain the license and credits;
provenance.json records the exact artifact hashes and regeneration steps.
crates/ox-core/src/grel/language.rs adapts its detection and text-processing
algorithms to Rust, with a sparse model, seeded Java-compatible randomness and
character tables generated from the reference APIs; no JVM is required at runtime.
Upstream credits Nakatani Shuyo, Fabian Kessler, Francois Roland, Robert Theis
and Elmer Garduno. Its original NGram source carries this notice:

  Copyright 2011 Nakatani Shuyo

The additional Commons mapping fixtures under tests/commons/ were generated by
running unmodified mapping classes from OpenRefine/CommonsExtension v0.1.5
(BSD 3-Clause License) with the OpenRefine libraries. Their provenance identifies
the exact source revision and hashes. The extension sources are fetched only
for regeneration and are not bundled with OxRefine. These synthetic cases check
cell/reconciliation mapping, not live Wikimedia Commons responses.
